    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>Closes a REAL security gap — Office endpoints currently ship with authorization filters stubbed (`// TODO: Task 033`). Applying `.AddOfficeAuthFilter()`/`.AddJobOwnershipFilter()`/`.AddEntityAccessFilter()` gates the endpoints. Security-sensitive auth change on the BFF; `bff-api` + `auth` tags trigger FULL rigor; must respect ADR-003/008 (endpoint-filter authorization) and BFF §10 governance.</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>W7</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Touches `Api/Office/OfficeEndpoints.cs` + filter wiring only — disjoint from other W7 tasks (add-in client, subscription manager, index config). The filter CLASSES already exist; this is wiring, not new filter logic. Runs anytime after W0.</parallel-reason>
    <fr-refs>FR-25</fr-refs>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Apply the already-authored BFF Office authorization filters to close the stubbed-auth security gap. Per spec FR-25 (and Owner Clarification: the filter CLASSES already ship on `master`), `OfficeEndpoints.cs` currently has authorization stubbed at lines ~172, ~471, ~490, ~761 (`// TODO: Task 033`). Replace each stub with the appropriate filter registration:
    - `.AddOfficeAuthFilter()` — baseline Office-caller authentication
    - `.AddJobOwnershipFilter()` — job-scoped endpoints (caller owns the job)
    - `.AddEntityAccessFilter()` — entity-scoped endpoints (caller has access to the target record)

    Choose the correct filter per endpoint based on what it does (baseline vs job-scoped vs entity-scoped). Do NOT author new filter logic — the classes exist; this task WIRES them. Any endpoint mapped unconditionally must have its filter/service registered unconditionally (per RB-T028 asymmetric-registration rule; ADR-032 Null-Object if a dependency is feature-gated).

    After wiring, add/adjust tests proving each protected endpoint rejects unauthorized callers (401/403) and admits authorized ones.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke BFF engineer authoritative on `Api/Office/OfficeEndpoints.cs`, the endpoint-filter authorization pattern (ADR-008), the existing Office filter classes, and the binding `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` governance (including the asymmetric-registration sub-mechanisms).
  </role>

  <goal>
    All four stubbed authorization sites in `OfficeEndpoints.cs` apply the correct filter (`.AddOfficeAuthFilter()`/`.AddJobOwnershipFilter()`/`.AddEntityAccessFilter()`); no `// TODO: Task 033` remains. Tests prove protected endpoints reject unauthorized callers and admit authorized ones. Build + tests green; publish-size + CVE reported; placement justification stated.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      The Outlook add-in calls BFF Office endpoints, but their authorization was left stubbed pending the auth-v2 foundation. That foundation (filter classes) now ships on `master`. This is a REAL security gap — the endpoints are currently under-protected. This task is the BFF half of FR-25 (task 072 migrates the add-in client; task 074 adds engine suggestions to the save pane).
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Office/OfficeEndpoints.cs (PRIMARY — stubs at ~172/471/490/761)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Office/ (existing filter classes `AddOfficeAuthFilter`/`AddJobOwnershipFilter`/`AddEntityAccessFilter`)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Program.cs (endpoint + DI registration)</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md (asymmetric-registration rule)</file>
      <file>tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ (endpoint auth tests)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec FR-25">Apply the stubbed Office auth filters at `OfficeEndpoints.cs` lines ~172/471/490/761 (filter classes already exist); Office endpoints protected.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-008">Authorization via endpoint filters, not middleware.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Auth seams — respect the central authorization primitives.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Do NOT author new filter logic — the classes exist; wire them. Pick the correct filter per endpoint's scope (baseline/job/entity).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project (§10 asymmetric registration)">Unconditionally-mapped endpoints have unconditional filter/service registration (RB-T028); ADR-032 Null-Object if a dependency is feature-gated.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-08">Add/update tests in `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/` proving each protected endpoint's authorization.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project (§10)">Load `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`; state Placement Justification; run `/conflict-check` before PR; report publish-size (baseline ~49.63 MB, ceiling 60 MB) + CVE.</constraint>
  </constraints>

