  <steps>
    <step order="1" name="Context check">Check context usage; handoff + stop if &gt; 70%.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Load knowledge">Read spec FR-25, ADR-008/003/032, bff-extensions.md (asymmetric-registration), endpoint-filters pattern.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Conflict check">Run `/conflict-check` for `Api/Office/**` before editing.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Inspect stubs + filters">Read `OfficeEndpoints.cs` at each stub (~172/471/490/761); understand each endpoint's scope. Read the existing filter classes to confirm their contracts.</step>
    <step order="5" name="Wire filters">Replace each `// TODO: Task 033` with the correct filter: baseline → `.AddOfficeAuthFilter()`; job-scoped → `.AddJobOwnershipFilter()`; entity-scoped → `.AddEntityAccessFilter()`. Ensure any required service is registered unconditionally (ADR-032 Null-Object if feature-gated).</step>
    <step order="6" name="Tests">Add/adjust tests: each protected endpoint rejects an unauthorized caller (401/403) and admits an authorized one. Verify unconditional registration for unconditionally-mapped endpoints (RB-T028).</step>
    <step order="7" name="Build + test">`dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` and `dotnet test tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ --filter Office`. Fix failures.</step>
    <step order="8" name="Publish-size + CVE">`dotnet publish -c Release ... -o deploy/api-publish/`; report absolute + delta vs ~49.63 MB (ceiling 60 MB). `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive`; confirm no new HIGH CVE.</step>
    <step order="9.5" name="FULL quality gates">Invoke `code-review` (auth focus); invoke `adr-check` against spec.md (ADR-008/003/032; NFR-08). Address Critical findings.</step>
    <step order="10" name="Update tracking">Mark task 073 ✅ in `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`. PR carries Placement Justification + publish-size delta + CVE.</step>
    <step order="11" name="Reset state">Update `current-task.md`: status → completed; advance; record decisions.</step>
  </steps>

